This directory contains the subset of the upstream `spai/models` package that
inference needs, vendored by TruePixels.rgb on 2026-09-12. TruePixels.rgb does
NOT train, fine-tune or otherwise alter the published weights.

Files and their relationship to upstream
----------------------------------------
filters.py            spai/models/filters.py, verbatim.
vision_transformer.py spai/models/vision_transformer.py, verbatim except that
                      the `timm.models.layers` import is replaced by
                      `layers.py` (see below).
sid.py                spai/models/sid.py, REDUCED to the classes the released
                      `spai.pth` checkpoint uses: PatchBasedMFViT, MFViT,
                      FrequencyRestorationEstimator, FeatureSpecificProjector,
                      Projector, ClassificationHead, FeatureImportanceProjector,
                      build_mf_vit, _init_weights, plus patchify_image from
                      spai/models/utils.py. Removed: ONNX export methods,
                      attention-mask export, CLIP/DINOv2 backbones, the
                      "single_extraction" model family, and the
                      DenseIntermediateFeaturesProcessor variants.
                      `einops.rearrange` calls replaced by equivalent
                      reshape/permute; `torchvision.transforms.Normalize` and
                      `torchvision.transforms.functional.five_crop` replaced by
                      equivalents in layers.py. No arithmetic was changed.
layers.py             NEW. Minimal replacements for the timm / torchvision /
                      einops symbols the upstream code imports.
config.py             NEW. The upstream yacs configuration (spai/config.py
                      defaults merged with configs/spai.yaml) transcribed as a
                      plain attribute tree, restricted to the keys the model
                      builders read. Values were cross-checked against the
                      config embedded in the released checkpoint.

Every local edit inside a vendored file is marked with a `# TruePixels:` comment.
